  "name": "technical-project-management",
  "description": "Manage technical projects from initiation through delivery and closure: choose and tailor predictive, iterative, Scrum, flow-based, or hybrid approaches; coordinate teams and vendors; track milestones, risks, issues, dependencies, forecasts, scope changes, and recovery. Use when a team has no project manager, a TPM needs decision-ready analysis, a project is slipping, or commitments and handoffs need coordination. Use `technical-program-management` instead when multiple related projects, teams, vendors, shared capacity, or benefits must be coordinated toward one outcome. Adapt depth to the user's expertise. Do not use for a standalone coding task, product discovery or strategy, only writing an implementation plan, only diagnosing Kanban flow, operating a ticket tool, incident command, or a release go/no-go decision; route those to specialists.",
